  "zh": "# 摩尔线程股价闪崩，OpenAI发布「非人思维」研究\n\n## AI与科技\n- **摩尔线程早盘触及20cm跌停**：国产GPU龙头罕见一字跌停，此前获大基金注资的明星股突然闪崩，提醒芯片概念股风险不容忽视。\n- **RTX 5090显卡价格暴涨**：黄牛囤货叠加货源紧张，高端AI训练显卡溢价严重，普通消费者几乎无卡可买。\n- **OpenAI回应wiki事件**：OpenAI与维基百科的数据使用争议持续发酵，AI训练数据版权问题再次成为行业焦点。\n\n## 技术与突破\n- **OpenAI发布An Alien Mind研究**：探讨大语言模型的独特推理方式，论文揭示AI思维与人类认知的本质差异。\n- **电子皮肤让假肢感知温度压力**：华盛顿州立大学突破性进展，义肢患者首次获得接近真实的触觉反馈。\n- **Isar Aerospace卫星入轨成功**：欧洲私营航天公司第二次发射即实现入轨部署，标志着欧洲航天商业化加速。\n\n## 行业与市场\n- **央视曝光水质检测企业造假**：多家机构被曝出具虚假报告，环保监测领域AI数据可信度引发公众质疑。\n- **AI能检查出自己的错误吗**：B站技术圈热议大模型自我纠错能力上限，这一问题的答案将直接影响AI落地可靠性。",
  "en": "# China's Top GPU Maker Crashes 20% as OpenAI Publishes Alien Mind Research\n\n## AI & Tech\n- **Moore Threads Stock Hits 20% Limit Down**: China's leading domestic GPU maker suffered a rare circuit-breaker crash, a stark reminder that chip concept stocks carry extreme volatility even after receiving state fund backing.\n- **RTX 5090 Graphics Card Prices Surge**: Severe supply shortages and scalping have pushed high-end AI training cards to absurd premiums, pricing average consumers out entirely.\n- **OpenAI Responds to Wiki Data Controversy**: Ongoing dispute over training data usage intensifies as copyright questions around AI training face renewed scrutiny.\n\n## Breakthroughs\n- **OpenAI Releases 'An Alien Mind' Research**: A deep dive into how large language models reason differently from humans, revealing fundamental cognitive gaps between AI and human intelligence.\n- **Electronic Skin Gives Prosthetics Temperature and Pressure Sense**: Washington State University breakthrough enables amputees to feel touch with near-natural fidelity for the first time.\n- **Isar Aerospace Reaches Orbit on Second Attempt**: European private launch company successfully deployed payloads on its second flight, marking a major milestone for commercial European spaceflight.\n\n## Industry & Society\n- **China CCTV Exposes Water Testing Fraud**: Multiple testing firms caught fabricating environmental data, raising serious questions about AI reliability in critical monitoring systems.\n- **Can AI Actually Catch Its Own Mistakes?**: Tech community debates the true limits of self-correction in large models—a question with massive implications for real-world AI deployment."
